A54 — the compositor stops waking when nothing is pending

After every timer wakeup steamcompmgr re-armed the vblank timer
unconditionally ("just in case the page-flip handler doesn't happen"), so the
loop ran at the full grid rate for the whole session: epoll, X dispatch, the
frame-callback walk over every window, presentation feedback, the mangoapp
publish and the cursor checks, with only the composite skipped. On the
Retroid Pocket 6 that was ~1500 wakeups and 6-9 % of a core on gamescope-xwm,
whatever the frame count.

The re-arm now runs on every pass of the loop, not only timer ones, and only
while there is work for the next wakeup:

- a repaint is pending (hasRepaint, a non-base-plane repaint, a forced
  repaint, a forwarded VR overlay) or a focus is fading out;
- a flip is in flight;
- a window has a done commit whose frame callback (or the limiter's release
  of it) has not gone out, or a done commit is held for a later vblank (FIFO,
  a desired present time);
- the cursor is shown and its auto-hide time has not passed (plus 100 ms, so
  the wakeup that hides it is never the one that stops);
- VRR is active or PipeWire is streaming (both keep the old behaviour).

After vblank_idle_ticks (default 2) timer wakeups with none of that, the
timer stays off until the next nudge. The page-flip handler still re-arms on
every flip, so the wakeup after a flip always runs. vblank_idle_ticks 0
restores the old always-armed behaviour.

Everything that set hasRepaint from another thread without waking the loop
now wakes it, or it would wait for an unrelated wakeup: cursor motion and
buttons (wlserver_oncursorevent), the cursor hide (wlserver_mousehide), the
set_look ConCommand and gamescope_control set_look / unset_look (through the
new wlserver_request_repaint: set, and nudge once per painted frame), and
screenshots (CScreenshotManager::TakeScreenshot). gamescope_private commands
repaint through A53's force_repaint.

A commit that becomes done while the compositor is idle takes its earliest
present time from the next grid point, not the last wakeup's target, which
is in the past after an idle stretch; the present margin (earliest present
minus latch, unsigned) no longer wraps when the two cross.

With vblank_debug on, idle/resume transitions are logged (rate-limited).

